  <h2 id="hook-redirect" set:html={t('docsConfiguration.hookRedirectTitle')} />

  <p set:html={t('docsConfiguration.hookRedirectDesc')} />
  <pre><code># ~/.lean-ctx/config.toml
redirect_exclude = [".wolf/**", ".claude/**", "*.json", "CLAUDE.md"]</code></pre>

  <pre><code># Or via environment variable (takes precedence)
export LEAN_CTX_HOOK_EXCLUDE=".wolf/**,.claude/**,*.json"</code></pre>

  <h3 id="agent-modes">Agent Integration Modes</h3>
  <p>
    <code>lean-ctx init --agent &lt;tool&gt;</code> supports two integration modes:
    <code>hybrid</code> (MCP reads + shell hooks, recommended) and <code>mcp</code> (explicit <code>ctx_*</code> tools only).
    <code>auto</code> selects the best default per tool (Hybrid for agents with shell access, MCP for others).
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`# Auto (recommended — selects Hybrid for most agents)
lean-ctx init --agent cursor

# Force MCP tools only
lean-ctx init --agent cursor --mode mcp

# Force Hybrid (MCP reads + shell compression)
lean-ctx init --agent cursor --mode hybrid`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Binary File Passthrough (v2.21.0)</h3>
  <p>
    The hook redirect automatically detects binary files (images, PDFs, archives, fonts, videos,
    compiled files) by extension and passes them through to the native Read tool. This ensures
    AI agents can still view screenshots, images, and other non-text files without interference.
  </p>

